{"last_link_id": 116, "nodes": [{"showAdvanced": true, "outputs": [{"name": "CONDITIONING", "links": [65, 68], "label": "CONDITIONING", "type": "CONDITIONING", "localized_name": "CONDITIONING"}, {"name": "seconds", "links": [66], "label": "seconds", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_name": "seconds"}], "color": "#232", "widgets_values": ["### Global Metadata\n\n**Basic Attributes:** BPM 132, E major. Mandopop / Children's Electronic Pop with folk-pop storytelling elements. Chinese-language vocal.\n\n**Global Emotional Progression:** The song opens on a bright, sunlit playful atmosphere — a kitten's mischief in a warm living room. Verses use conversational, rhythmic storytelling to introduce each character (the cat, the big dog, the small dog) with gentle humor. Pre-choruses steadily build anticipation as the three animals converge. Choruses explode into exuberant, celebratory group energy — catchy, warm, and irresistibly cute. The bridge strips back for a quirky, goofy interlude of character banter and physical comedy, then the final chorus delivers maximum warmth and joy, resolving on a tender, sleepy goodnight.\n\n**Application Scenarios & Imagery:** Children's animation, pet daily vlogs, cute short-video background music. Imagery: afternoon sunlight through a window, a yarn ball rolling across the floor, a big dog lazily flicking its tail, a tiny puppy bouncing and yapping, a kitten arching its back then instantly melting into a cuddle.\n\n**Sonics & Production Profile:** Wide, bright, polished soundstage with sparkling upper-mids and highs. Tight, bouncy low end — controlled, not booming. Moderate compression maintains radio-ready energy while preserving percussive transients. Playful sound-effect layers are intentionally kept slightly raw and characterful to preserve a goofy, handmade charm rather than over-polishing.\n\n---\n\n### Vocal Details\n\n**Vocal Gender & Timbre:** Lead: a single female vocalist with a bright, clear, youthful soprano — crisp articulation, naturally cheerful and slightly mischievous. Character harmony layers: a low, warm male voice (representing the big dog) and a high, childlike voice (representing the small dog) appear in choruses and the bridge, creating a three-character \"group vocal\" effect.\n\n**Vocal Style:** Verses use a conversational, semi-spoken rhythmic delivery — like telling a funny pet story, with playful inflection and bouncy phrasing. Pre-choruses rise melodically with increasing energy. Choruses open into full, bright pop singing — anthemic, catchy, warm. The bridge features melodized onomatopoeia (meows, barks, whines) sung in character — goofy and expressive but never harsh or shrill. The outro softens to a gentle, sleepy murmur.\n\n**Harmony/Backing Vocals:** Choruses feature multi-tracked self-harmonies in parallel thirds and octaves — full, choir-like, celebratory. Pre-choruses use unison doubling to build anticipation. The bridge layers the three character voices in call-and-response banter — low male, high child, and lead soprano interjecting like animals arguing then making up.\n\n**Vocal FX:** Lead vocal: moderate short-delay reverb + transparent pitch correction for a clean modern pop sheen. Chorus harmonies: wider stereo spread + slightly more reverb for spaciousness. Bridge onomatopoeia section: subtle telephone-filter and pitch-shift effects to enhance comedic character. Outro: gentle low-pass filter to suggest falling asleep.\n\n---\n\n### Arrangement\n\n**Instrument Lifecycle (Primary / Secondary Layering):**\n\n- **Primary:** A bright, percussive plucked synth (ukulele/pipa-like timbre) carries the central melodic hook from bar 1 through the entire track — the song's signature identity. Glockenspiel/celesta doubles the hook in choruses for extra cuteness.\n- **Secondary:** A warm, rounded synth bass enters at Verse 1, locking with the kick in a bouncy, syncopated pattern. Airy synth pads swell in pre-choruses and fully open in choruses. A soft acoustic guitar strum is layered in Verse 2 for organic warmth.\n\n**Groove & Foundation Progression (section-by-section):**\n\n- **[Intro] (0:00–0:08):** Plucked synth alone + soft shaker, with one melodized cat-meow sample as a hook. Kick enters at bar 3.\n- **[Verse 1] (0:08–0:30):** Stripped groove — four-on-the-floor kick, snare on 2 & 4, closed hi-hats, bouncy bass. Woodblock/agogo percussion accents the \"妙脆角\" rhythmic motif. Lead vocal takes center.\n- **[Pre-Chorus] (0:30–0:42):** Density increases — open hi-hats, tambourine, pads swelling. Melodic line ascends. A low dog-woof sample pads the bottom.\n- **[Chorus] (0:42–1:06):** Full energy — kick + layered claps + snare + auxiliary percussion (shaker, woodblock, tambourine all active). Plucked synth + glockenspiel dual melody. Bass most active. Three-character group harmonies. Peak joy.\n- **[Verse 2] (1:06–1:28):** Same as Verse 1 but with added acoustic guitar strum and a melodized puppy-bark sample as rhythmic fill.\n- **[Pre-Chorus] (1:28–1:40):** Same as first, with big-dog low \"woof\" harmony under the vocal.\n- **[Chorus] (1:40–2:04):** Full energy, sustained.\n- **[Bridge] (2:04–2:26):** Groove halves / strips back — only plucked synth, soft piano, and light percussion. Three character voices alternate melodized onomatopoeia in call-and-response (cat meow → big dog woof → puppy yap → all together), comedic and chaotic. Last 2 bars: drum fill builds tension.\n- **[Chorus] (2:26–2:54):** Maximum energy — all instruments + all harmonies + a collective \"meow-woof\" cheer sample. Warmest, fullest climax.\n- **[Outro] (2:54–3:08):** Fades to plucked synth + soft piano + a contented purr sample. Gentle \"晚安啦\" vocal, clean resolved ending.\n\n**Embellishments, Textures & Spatial FX:**\n\n- Melodized animal sound effects throughout (cat meow, dog bark, purr) — all pitch-corrected and rhythmically placed, serving as percussion/fills, never noise.\n- Transitions: risers, reverse cymbals, \"whoosh\" effects synced to character entrances.\n- Bridge: subtle tape-stop / vinyl crackle texture for retro-goofy flavor.\n- Occasional \"ding-dong\" doorbell or \"pop\" bubble sounds in choruses for extra playfulness.\n- Spatial: lead vocal center; plucked synth slightly left; glockenspiel slightly right; pads wide; animal effects randomly panned to create a \"running all around the room\" feel.", "[Intro]\n[Verse 1]\n妙脆角小猫 弓背炸毛\n尾巴翘得像个小问号\n踮起脚尖 偷偷瞄\n毛线球就是它的宝\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n墙角那边 谁在睡觉\n大狗翻身 尾巴扫扫\n小狗蹦跳 汪汪叫\n一场好戏 就要开演了\n\n[Chorus]\n喵～妙脆角小猫 喵喵喵\n大狗汪汪 小狗跳跳\n三个伙伴 吵吵闹闹\n温馨的家里 充满欢笑\n\n[Verse 2]\n大狗懒洋洋 趴在墙角\n尾巴一扫 把花瓶碰倒\n小狗蹦蹦跳 汪汪叫\n追着小猫 满屋跑\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n小猫跳上 沙发靠背\n大狗抬头 张大嘴\n小狗转圈 追自己尾\n你追我赶 谁也不累\n\n[Chorus]\n喵～妙脆角小猫 喵喵喵\n大狗汪汪 小狗跳跳\n三个伙伴 吵吵闹闹\n温馨的家里 充满欢笑\n\n[Bridge]\n小猫炸毛 大狗傻笑\n小狗转圈 自己摔倒\n你追我赶 好不热闹\n累了就一起 睡个大觉\n\n[Chorus]\n喵～妙脆角小猫 喵喵喵\n大狗汪汪 小狗跳跳\n三个伙伴 吵吵闹闹\n温馨的家里 永远美好\n\n[Outro]\n喵～汪～汪汪～喵～\n晚安啦\n", 222, "fixed", 180, 1.7, 50], "inputs": [{"name": "clip", "link": 64, "label": "clip", "type": "CLIP", "localized_name": "clip"}, {"widget": {"name": "caption"}, "name": "caption", "label": "caption", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "caption"}, {"widget": {"name": "lyrics"}, "name": "lyrics", "label": "lyrics", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "lyrics"}, {"widget": {"name": "seed"}, "name": "seed", "link": 73, "label": "seed", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "seed"}, {"widget": {"name": "max_duration"}, "name": "max_duration", "label": "max_duration", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_name": "max_duration"}, {"widget": {"name": "cfg_scale"}, "name": "cfg_scale", "label": "cfg_scale", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_name": "cfg_scale"}, {"widget": {"name": "top_k"}, "name": "top_k", "label": "top_k", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "top_k"}], "flags": {}, "type": "MiniMaxMusic3TextEncode", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#353", "size": [320.9012451171875, 479.4555358886719], "pos": [0, 0], "id": 45, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.31.0", "ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable